From: Dict Xiong <me@dxng.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: drop monitor-only decapsulated RX frames

RX_FLAG_ONLY_MONITOR tells mac80211 not to process a frame on regular
interfaces. Frames with RX_FLAG_8023 bypass ieee80211_rx_monitor(),
including its ONLY_MONITOR check, and can therefore reach the Ethernet
data path despite that flag. In particular, mt76 can set ONLY_MONITOR
after rejecting a frame's packet number without clearing RX_FLAG_8023.

Honor the flag before forwarding or delivering a decapsulated frame.
The raw 802.11 monitor path is unchanged. This only fixes frames handled
by mac80211; it does not deduplicate traffic forwarded entirely in
hardware.

Signed-off-by: Dict Xiong <me@dxng.cn>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
---
--- a/net/mac80211/rx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/rx.c
@@ -5274,6 +5274,10 @@
 	rx.link_id = -1;
 
 	I802_DEBUG_INC(local->dot11ReceivedFragmentCount);
+
+	/* Decapsulated monitor-only frames must not enter the data path. */
+	if (unlikely(status->flag & RX_FLAG_ONLY_MONITOR))
+		goto drop;
 
 	/* drop frame if too short for header */
 	if (skb->len < sizeof(struct ethhdr))
